SUMMARY:Montclair Film Festival - Kill. Bury. Print.
DESCRIPTION:KILL. BURY. PRINT. tackles brazen corruption and press intimidation in remote southeast Oklahoma. When a small family-run newspaper begins reporting on allegations of sex\, drugs\, and violence within the county sheriff’s office\, they find themselves the target of the sheriff’s retaliation. As tensions escalate\, the paper secretly records the sheriff and local officials musing about killing and burying them\, turning a local story into national news. Ben Klein’s film is a timely and powerful story of the relationship between journalists and those in power\, a look at how corruption threatens our access to the truth. \nQ&A with Director Ben Klein and Producer Rachel Maddow follows the screening. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
