SUMMARY:Cassandra: An Ongoing Tragedy\, presented by Mosaic Dance Theater Company
DESCRIPTION:Rich with emotional and social relevance\, “Cassandra: An Ongoing Tragedy” by Ruth Cantrell contrasts Greek myths to modern day tragedies – war\, terrorism\, racism\, sexual assault\, gun violence\, depicting the eternal existence of hate\, and exploring the impact of the evils brought forth from Pandora’s Box. The stories in this piece are related by fictional characters in historical situations\, through spoken word and dance\, with an original score. Cast of 11. Oct 16 at 7pm\, Oct 17 at 5pm\, Oct 18 at 3pm.\nCONTENT WARNING\nThis production shows graphic images of violence\, including warfare\, bombings\, and their victims\, with intense\, jarring audio of gunfire and explosions. It is intended for mature audiences and those seeking to understand the events. Please take care of your well-being. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
